# Streams a cartesian path to the robot over the DIPC queue, one robtarget at a
# time. The goal ends when the robot has arrived, not when the last point has
# been queued.
#
# Cancelling does not stop the robot: the point being sent is promoted to the
# last one, the queue runs to its end, and the goal reports CANCELED once the
# robot stands still.

# MoveL or MoveJ - which RAPID routine draws the path.
string motion_command
# TCP speed in mm/s, as text. RAPID clamps it to 5-1000.
string speed
# Poses in metres, the ROS convention, converted to the millimetres a robtarget
# holds. Orientation is a ROS quaternion (x,y,z,w) and becomes ABB's (w,x,y,z);
# the arm configuration is left to the controller.
geometry_msgs/PoseArray path
---
bool success
string message
# Points RAPID reported as done. After an abort this can be a point or two
# ahead of where the robot physically stopped: the planner runs ahead.
int32 executed_count
---
int32 current_index
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped current_pose
string state
